From b1b92f0fa06a462e117a09ed703bfbc3b8b6d1ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:34:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] ci-review bot: retry a failed review-status
 download; a failed targeted refresh marks the comment and queues one
 re-refresh

PR #1661 (head 8543d56, approved, required CI green at 18:23:53Z) waited 45 min on a
"running on 8543d56" ci-review-bot comment. Its CI-completion refresh (run 43279407344,
18:24:09Z) logged "PR #1661: ERROR review-status artifact download failed" and went red.
Every review-status artifact of CI run 43276201639 existed by then (newest
review-status-ci-timings, created 18:23:46Z), so this was a transient download error, not a
missing artifact. Nothing retried it until a hand dispatch at 19:07Z (run 43286827504).
The 200 newest bot runs show the same error three times (#1617 17:26Z, #1480 18:27Z,
#1661 18:24Z).

- live_comment.fetch_all_review_statuses: an optional retry_delays budget shared by the
  whole call. _download_artifact records why it failed (last_download_error), and the
  strict error names the artifact, the cause and the attempt count.
- batch_review_comments: a targeted refresh retries for about 90 s (5+10+15+25+35); the sweep
  shares the retry with 15 s per PR and is otherwise unchanged. If a targeted refresh
  still cannot build the snapshot, it:
  * queues exactly one delayed re-refresh, but only when CI triggered the refresh. It
    sends a workflow_dispatch with head_sha, delay_seconds=300 and retry_of=<run>, and a
    dispatched refresh never queues another;
  * marks the comment: the footer becomes "refresh failed on <head> at <time> (<error>);
    one re-refresh queued for ~HH:MM UTC, then hourly" (or "next refresh: hourly sweep"),
    and the state line gets failed=<stamp>. hermes-core-wt-land's BOT_HEAD parser then
    reads neither "running" nor "ran", and readers see why. A completed "ran on" snapshot
    of the same head is kept. Ordering and head-race checks apply as for a normal write.
- workflow: workflow_dispatch inputs head_sha/delay_seconds/retry_of, passed through env
  only (the script validates the 40-hex sha and a digits-only delay capped at 600 s);
  actions: write (to dispatch); a per-head "-retry-<sha>" concurrency group.

Tests (tests/ci/test_batch_review_comments.py): 9 new tests, RED on base (9 failed, 48
passed) and GREEN on the head (57 passed). They cover (a) fails twice, then posts "ran on";
(b) always fails: run red, failed marker, exactly one dispatch; the re-refresh never
re-dispatches; the sweep writes no marker; a write failure is not a failed refresh; a
dispatched delay is capped; the workflow shape. (c) The existing tests stay green, as do
tests/ci/test_live_comment.py and the rest of tests/ci (apart from one unrelated
promisor-fetch failure in test_plugin_catalog_ci_confinement).

Card: t_01a1d1292db9d3cb
